          "unit_id": "new_flatmate",
          "title": "The New Flatmate",
          "description": "Describe personas, cosas y lugares con oraciones de relativo: who, which, that, where, whose.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "new_flatmate_lesson",
              "title": "Relative clauses",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "The new flatmate",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "Hi! I'm Ollie, Mrs Green's nephew."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "Welcome, Ollie. This is the kitchen, where we spend most of our time."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "And this is the garden that Priya looks after. Those are her famous tomatoes."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "Wow. And who's the guy who's singing upstairs?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "That's Sam, the flatmate who's leaving. His room is the one you'd have."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "Is it the room which looks over the garden?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Yes, that's it. It's the best room in the house."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "What's the area like? Is there a place where I can go running?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Brandon Hill is five minutes away. It's the park where we play football."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "Perfect. By the way, I work at a restaurant that serves Spanish food."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Spanish food? Then you're the flatmate we've been looking for!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "When can you move in?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "At the beginning of August, when Sam leaves."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "A week later, Ollie comes to see the room. He's twenty-six, he's from Manchester, and he works in a restaurant which opened last year in Bristol."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"the flatmate who's leaving\": we use who for…",
                        "options": [
                          "people",
                          "things",
                          "places"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"the room which looks over the garden\": we use which for…",
                        "options": [
                          "things",
                          "people"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"the park where we play football\": we use where for…",
                        "options": [
                          "places",
                          "people"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"the flatmate we've been looking for\" has no who. Why?",
                        "options": [
                          "It's the object of the verb.",
                          "It's the subject of the verb."
                        ],
                        "answer": 0,
                        "explanation": "Podemos omitir who/which/that cuando no son el sujeto de la oración de relativo."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Relative clauses",
                    "explanation": "Las oraciones de relativo especifican de qué persona, cosa o lugar hablamos:\n• who → personas: Sam is the flatmate who's leaving.\n• which → cosas: It's the room which looks over the garden.\n• that → personas o cosas (más informal): the garden that Priya looks after.\n• where → lugares: the park where we play football.\n• whose → posesión: Ollie is the man whose aunt is Mrs Green.\n\nSi el pronombre es el objeto de la oración (no el sujeto), se puede omitir: the flatmate (who) we've been looking for. Si es el sujeto, no: the flatmate who's leaving.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Pronombre",
                        "Para",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "who",
                          "personas",
                          "Sam is the flatmate who's leaving."
                        ],
                        [
                          "which",
                          "cosas",
                          "It's the room which looks over the garden."
                        ],
                        [
                          "that",
                          "personas o cosas",
                          "the garden that Priya looks after"
                        ],
                        [
                          "where",
                          "lugares",
                          "the park where we play football"
                        ],
                        [
                          "whose",
                          "posesión",
                          "Ollie is the man whose aunt is Mrs Green."
                        ],
                        [
                          "(omitido)",
                          "cuando es objeto",
                          "the flatmate (who) we've been looking for"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "This is the kitchen, where we spend most of our time.",
                      "And this is the garden that Priya looks after.",
                      "That's Sam, the flatmate who's leaving.",
                      "Then you're the flatmate we've been looking for!"
                    ]
                  }
                },
